  "task": "Embedding geometry analysis: test whether node2vec dimensions are near-parallel (low effective rank PR) compared to SVD-based methods",
  "method": "Participation ratio PR = (\u03a3\u03bb)\u00b2/\u03a3\u03bb\u00b2 of Gram matrix; off-diagonal cosine similarity; N=2000 SBM, 10 samples, dim=64",
  "result_summary": "HYPOTHESIS CONFIRMED: Node2Vec has dramatically lower PR (PR≈23.7 at mu=0.40) vs. all SVD/spectral methods (PR≈64.0, perfectly orthogonal). Node2Vec dimensions are near-parallel with mean off-diagonal |cos|=0.122, while SVD methods have mean |cos|≈0.0001 (essentially orthogonal). The community signal for node2vec is concentrated in ~24 effective dimensions rather than all 64, confirming the original idea.md hypothesis. Importantly, gradient_weight_svd and clip_0_svd match or exceed node2vec NMI (0.379/0.370 vs 0.350 at mu=0.40) WITHOUT near-parallel dimensions — so near-parallelism is a property of the SGNS optimization geometry, not required for community detection.",
